## Fare estimate — deleted everywhere

- **Route panel** ([routePanel.js](frontend/client/js/routePanel.js)): the "Fare estimate" row is gone; the panel now shows Origin → Destination → Distance → Major stops. Verified live in the DOM: zero fare/MAD text anywhere on the page.
- **Route popups** ([routes.js](frontend/client/js/routes.js)) and the status line wording ("verify route and fare locally" → "verify the route locally").
- **Backend**: `fareEstimate` removed from the [Route schema](backend/models/Route.js), the [seed data](backend/scripts/seed-routes.js), and POST-payload [validation](backend/controllers/route.controller.js). Mongoose's strict schema means even legacy Atlas documents that still physically contain the field can no longer appear in API responses.
- **Scaffold copies** for consistency: [App.jsx](frontend/client/src/App.jsx), [casaway.html](frontend/client/public/casaway.html). A repo-wide grep finds **zero** remaining fare references in client code.

## UI/UX bugs found while rechecking — and fixed

1. **Dismissed install banner kept reappearing** — `display:flex` in CSS beat the `hidden` attribute. Added `.install-banner[hidden] { display:none; }`; verified it now stays hidden after dismissal (and still shows for a fresh visitor).
2. **Map clicks never selected a station** — [markers.js](frontend/client/js/markers.js) invokes `onSelect(station.id)` but [app.js](frontend/client/app.js) treated the argument as a station object, so every map-marker click called `selectStation(undefined)`. Fixed the signature; verified with a real click on Tit Mellil: row activates, route list filters to exactly "Garage Allal to Tit Mellil", trace draws.
3. **Destination depots showed an empty "Destinations" line** — destinations are now built **bidirectionally** (arrival depots list their incoming routes with short labels like "Derb Omar"), the destination matcher handles short names vs. long canonical names (name → district → substring), and the row hides itself when empty. Verified: Oulfa popup shows "Maarif · Derb Omar · Place de la Concorde"; selecting a destination-only station now filters its routes too.
4. **Service worker served stale CSS forever** — cache-first with a never-changing version, so no style fix ever reached returning users (this actually blocked my own verification). Bumped to `casaway-v3` and switched static assets to **stale-while-revalidate**; also fixed `warmShellCache` in app.js that still opened the old `v2` cache.
5. **Mobile dead strip** — a ~200px black gap sat below the map (explicit `height: 60vh` blocked grid stretch); the map now fills to the footer.
6. **Mobile install banner was cramped** into three squeezed lines — now a full-width single row with safe-area padding.
7. **Accessibility**: `aria-expanded="true"` was hardcoded on the menu toggle while the drawer starts closed — now `false`.

## Verified

Six clean `vite` builds; `node --check` passes on all five edited backend files; desktop and mobile browser passes (screenshots above) covering banner lifecycle, no-fare UI, popup contents, sidebar and map-click selection with route filtering; console has no app errors (only a Google geolocation-provider 403, which the app handles by silently remembering location-unavailable).

## Limitations

**MongoDB Atlas is unreachable from this machine right now** (DNS-level hang, environmental — it worked earlier today), so `/api/routes` hangs and I could not re-seed to physically purge the legacy `fareEstimate` fields from the Atlas collection. The UI was verified against the offline snapshot fallback, and the schema removal guarantees the API can't emit fares once connectivity returns. The backend server (with the new code) and the dev preview are still running. Changes are **not committed** — say the word and I'll push.
