Here's what the `useLeafletEvent` hook and related improvements accomplish:

#### 1. **`useLeafletEvent` Hook** (lines 13-24)
```javascript
function useLeafletEvent(map, eventName, handler, deps = []) {
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!map) return;
    const id = '__leaflet_event_' + eventName;
    map.on(eventName, handler);
    return () => {
      map.off(eventName, handler);
    };
  }, [map, eventName, ...deps]);
}
```
- Properly cleans up Leaflet event listeners on component unmount
- Prevents memory leaks and stale closures
- Follows React's `useEffect` cleanup pattern

#### 2. **Marker click cleanup** (line 388)
```javascript
// Use useLeafletEvent for click handler cleanup
useLeafletEvent(marker, 'click', () => {
  setSelectedStationId(station.id);
}, [station.id]);
```
- Each station marker's click handler now properly cleans up
- Prevents the marker from holding stale state after unmount

#### 3. **`escapeHtml` improved** (line 51)
```javascript
function escapeHtml(value) {
  const div = document.createElement('div');
  div.textContent = value || '';
  return div.innerHTML;
