The `.fare-widget` uses `background: var(--surface)` (solid surface). Inside the glass popup wrapper, this creates a solid card inside a glass frame. The `.leaflet-popup-content .fare-widget` at line 735 only adjusts margin/padding/gap — it doesn't change the background. 

For consistency, the fare widget inside popups should also get glass treatment. But actually, looking at the design: the popup wrapper IS the glass frame, and the fare widget inside being a slightly different surface (var(--surface) = `#0d121c`) creates a nice layered effect — a darker card on a lighter glass background. This is a valid design choice and matches what we see in the screenshot.

